# {{ .Name }} ({{ .Type | title }})

Get information about a Kerberos external authentication configured on the WALLIX Bastion.

## Example Usage

```terraform
# Look up an existing Kerberos external authentication by name
data "wallix-bastion_externalauth_kerberos" "corporate" {
  authentication_name = "corporate_kerberos"
}

# Reference it from another resource, e.g. an authentication domain
resource "wallix-bastion_authdomain_mapping" "kerberos_mapping" {
  domain_name = "corporate.local"
  auth_domain = data.wallix-bastion_externalauth_kerberos.corporate.authentication_name
}

# Output non-sensitive connection details
output "kerberos_kdc" {
  value = {
    host               = data.wallix-bastion_externalauth_kerberos.corporate.host
    ker_dom_controller = data.wallix-bastion_externalauth_kerberos.corporate.ker_dom_controller
    port               = data.wallix-bastion_externalauth_kerberos.corporate.port
  }
}
```

{{ .SchemaMarkdown | trimspace }}

## Usage Notes

### Lookup Key

`authentication_name` is the only Required argument and is used to look up the Kerberos external
authentication by its unique name on the Bastion. If no external authentication with that name
exists, the data source returns an error.

### Sensitive Fields Are Never Populated

The `keytab` attribute is marked `Sensitive` in the schema because a keytab is configured on the
resource, but like other secret material on the Bastion API, it is **never returned by a read**.
This data source will always report an empty value for `keytab` - do not rely on it to retrieve
the actual keytab content. If you need the keytab value in Terraform, it must come from your own
secret management system, not from this data source.

### Other Computed Attributes

- **host** / **ker_dom_controller** / **port**: KDC connection details.
- **kerberos_password**: `true` when the authentication type is password-based Kerberos
  (`KERBEROS-PASSWORD`); otherwise not set.
- **description**: free-form description configured on the resource.
- **login_attribute**: the LDAP/Kerberos attribute used to identify the login.
- **use_primary_auth_domain**: whether the primary authentication domain is used for this
  Kerberos configuration.
